otre Dame\n\nALGEBRAIC GEOMETRY AND COMMUTATIVE ALGEBRA SEMINAR\n\nSpeaker: Ada Stelzer  \nUniversity of Illinois Urbana-Champaign\n\nDate: Thursday, April 10, 2025  \nTime: 3:30 PM  \nLocation: 258 Hurley Bldg  \nZoom URL: NA\n\nLecture Title:  \nRSK as a linear operator\n\nAbstract\n\nThe Robinson-Schensted-Knuth correspondence (RSK) is a bijection of central importance in algebraic combinatorics, mapping nonnegative integer matrices to pairs (P, Q) of semistandard Young tableaux. This set-theoretic bijection extends to define a linear operator on the coordinate ring of the space of m by n matrices. The linear operator properties of RSK have received little study, despite the usefulness of this operator in several classical applications. In this talk, we will characterize the diagonalizability of the RSK linear operator in terms of Dynkin diagrams and present several results on its eigenvalues, trace, and determinant. Based on joint work with Alexander Yong, arXiv:2410.23009.\n\n<visual_element id=\"e1\">\nPortrait photo of Ada Stelzer, smiling, wearing a tie-dye shirt, against a blue studio backdrop.\n</visual_element>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGraph decompositions | Request PDF (https://www.researchgate.net/publication/329786822_Graph_decompositions)\nciteturn7search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: 20.9 years ago; Crawled: 3 months ago; A triangle design is balanced if all nonzero vectors are involved in the same number of triangles. ... We also prove that the existence of a triangle design over GF(2) invariant under the action of the Singer cycle group is equivalent to the existence of a partition of $Z_{2^n-1}\\backslash\\{0\\}$ into special 18-subsets and find such designs for n=7, 13, 19.\nWe define a triangle design as a partition of the set of 2-dimensional subspaces of an n-dimensional vector space into triangles, where a triangle consists of three subspaces with the trivial, 0-dimensional, intersection and 1-dimensional mutual intersections. A triangle design is balanced if all nonzero vectors are involved in the same number of triangles. Over the binary field GF(2), we construct balanced triangle designs for all admissible n (congruent to 1 modulo 6) and an infinite class of balanced block-divisible triangle designs. We also prove that the existence of a triangle design over GF(2) invariant under the action of the Singer cycle group is equivalent to the existence of a partition of $Z_{2^n-1}\\backslash\\{0\\}$ into special 18-subsets and find such designs for n=7, 13, 19.\n\nView\n\nShow abstract\n\n... Fixing a graph G, a natural problem that arises is to determine the spectrum for G-designs (or, more simply, for the graph G), which is the set of all n ∈ N such that a G-design of the order n exists. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nau:Stelzer_A in:math - SciRate Search (https://scirate.com/search?q=au%3AStelzer_A+in%3Amath)\nciteturn7search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 months ago; @misc{2506.13684, author = {Ada Stelzer}, title = {{S}ums of {S}chubert structure constants with bounded {C}oxeter length}, year = {2025}, eprint = {2506.13684}, note = {arXiv:2506.13684v1} }[Button: Copy Citation] ... Oct 31 2024 math.RA math.CO math.RT arXiv:2410.23009v2 ... We study it as a linear operator on the coordinate ring of matrices, proving results about its diagonalizability, eigenvalues, trace, and determinant.\n  * Sums of Schubert structure constants with bounded Coxeter length\n\nAda Stelzer\n\nJun 17 2025 math.CO math.RT arXiv:2506.13684v1\n\n[Button: Scited][Button: Scite!]\n\n1\n\n@misc{2506.13684, author = {Ada Stelzer}, title = {{S}ums of {S}chubert structure constants with bounded {C}oxeter length}, year = {2025}, eprint = {2506.13684}, note = {arXiv:2506.13684v1} }[Button: Copy Citation]\n\nPDF\n\nPak-Robichaux recently introduced a signed puzzle rule for Schubert structure constants, which they use to show that